Journey: An order for each EU ledger customer is priced from the ledger's price list
Tags: @postgres @db @ui
Risk: 2

# One run per row of the query (the row's columns are variables)
Log in as manager
Open /orders/new
Select "${customer_name}" from the Customer dropdown
Select "Gadget (49.50)" from the Product dropdown
Click the "Submit order" button
Expect the page contains "created"
Expect the page contains "${customer_name}"

# UI <-> DB: the order lines table compares with the ledger's price list, cell by cell
Capture the rows of the Order lines table as lines
Run query "PRICE_LIST_ROW" on ledger with sku="SKU-200" and store the rows as priced
Compare ${priced} with ${lines} by SKU

Examples: from query "EU_CUSTOMERS" on ledger with region="EU"
